---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { RELEASES, REPO, GETTING_STARTED, SECURITY, HELP } from '../../../../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Download | Bus Log Analyzer" description="Download Osvanta Bus Log Analyzer for Windows: a portable ZIP, no installer needed.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Download</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Bus Log Analyzer is a portable Windows application. It is free, and there is no installer.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href={RELEASES}>Get the latest release on GitHub</a>
    </div>

    <h2>Install and run</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>On the release page, download the file ending in <code>_Windows.zip</code>.</li>
      <li>Extract the ZIP to any folder you can write to. Administrator rights are not needed.</li>
      <li>Run <code>BusLogAnalyzer.exe</code>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      The executable is not code-signed yet, so Windows SmartScreen shows a warning the first time
      you start it. Choose <strong>More info</strong>, then <strong>Run anyway</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2>Check the download</h2>
    <p>
      Each release comes with a <code>SHA256SUMS.txt</code> file. In PowerShell, run
      <code>Get-FileHash</code> on the downloaded ZIP; it must print the hash that file lists.
      A software bill of materials (<code>sbom.cdx.json</code>, CycloneDX) lists every library the
      release was built with.
    </p>
    <p>Download the application only from the GitHub release page.</p>

    <h2>Next steps</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={GETTING_STARTED}>Getting started</a>: from a measurement file to your first plot in five minutes.</li>
      <li><a href={HELP}>Help</a>: every part of the tool in detail.</li>
      <li><a href={`${REPO}/releases`}>All releases</a> and what changed in each.</li>
      <li><a href={REPO}>Source code</a>, to build it yourself.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Removing it</h2>
    <p>
      Delete the application's folder, and <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Osvanta\BusLogAnalyzer</code> for
      its logs and settings. Nothing is written to the registry.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
